# * Built-in price fetching in get: this repo's extension, not upstream's

# get takes no --today, as in hledger, so most of these cases run it through
# import --get, which passes import's --today and --dry-run on to it (new.j,
# empty, gives import nothing to import). With --dry-run nothing is fetched.

# ** 1. Without a prices/getprices script, get fetches prices itself: for each
# commodity held in an asset or liability account, other than the base
# currency ($, declared CAD by its tag), and for usd, which btc is priced in.
# Each is asked for from 7 days before its first posting, or before that of a
# commodity priced in it, to yesterday, by Yahoo tickers tried in turn: two
# currencies' FX pair, the market code, a cryptocurrency's pair.
<
commodity $ ; price: CAD

2026-10-01 buy
    assets:broker      10 VEQT.TO @ $45
    assets:cash      $-450

2026-10-02 usd
    assets:usd        100 usd @ $1.40
    assets:cash      $-140

2026-10-05 btc
    assets:crypto     0.001 btc @ 72000 usd
    assets:usd        -72 usd

$ D=$(mktemp -d) && cd $D && touch new.j && hledger -f - import --get --dry-run --today 2026-11-12 new.j 2>&1; s=$?; cd /; rm -rf $D; exit $s
no ./data/getdata script, skipping data fetch
would run: yahoo VEQT.TO or VEQT.TO-CAD 2026-09-24..2026-11-11 >./prices/VEQT.TO.prices
would run: yahoo BTC or BTC-USD 2026-09-28..2026-11-11 >./prices/btc.prices
would run: yahoo USDCAD=X or USD or USD-CAD 2026-09-25..2026-11-11 >./prices/usd.prices
no new transactions found in new.j
>=0

# ** 2. Only missing days are asked for, those without a P directive in the
# journal or the price file, and of those only runs longer than 7 days or
# reaching yesterday: here not the 7 days before the first posting or the two
# weekends, but the 12 days from 2026-10-14 and the days since the last price.
<
P 2026-10-13 VEQT.TO $45.30

2026-10-05 buy
    assets:broker      10 VEQT.TO @ $45
    assets:cash      $-450

$ D=$(mktemp -d) && cd $D && touch new.j && mkdir prices && printf 'P 2026-10-05 VEQT.TO $45\nP 2026-10-06 VEQT.TO $45\nP 2026-10-07 VEQT.TO $45\nP 2026-10-08 VEQT.TO $45\nP 2026-10-09 VEQT.TO $45\nP 2026-10-12 VEQT.TO $45\nP 2026-10-26 VEQT.TO $46\nP 2026-10-27 VEQT.TO $46\nP 2026-10-28 VEQT.TO $46\nP 2026-10-29 VEQT.TO $46\nP 2026-10-30 VEQT.TO $46\nP 2026-11-02 VEQT.TO $46\nP 2026-11-03 VEQT.TO $46\nP 2026-11-04 VEQT.TO $46\nP 2026-11-05 VEQT.TO $46\nP 2026-11-06 VEQT.TO $46\n' >prices/VEQT.TO.prices && hledger -f - import --get --dry-run --today 2026-11-12 new.j 2>&1; s=$?; cd /; rm -rf $D; exit $s
no ./data/getdata script, skipping data fetch
would run: yahoo VEQT.TO or VEQT.TO-USD 2026-10-14..2026-10-25 >./prices/VEQT.TO.prices
would run: yahoo VEQT.TO or VEQT.TO-USD 2026-11-07..2026-11-11 >./prices/VEQT.TO.prices
no new transactions found in new.j
>=0

# ** 3. With every price in up to yesterday, but for a weekend, nothing is
# asked for.
<
2026-11-09 buy
    assets:broker      10 VEQT.TO @ $45
    assets:cash      $-450

$ D=$(mktemp -d) && cd $D && touch new.j && mkdir prices && printf 'P 2026-11-02 VEQT.TO $45\nP 2026-11-03 VEQT.TO $45\nP 2026-11-04 VEQT.TO $45\nP 2026-11-05 VEQT.TO $45\nP 2026-11-06 VEQT.TO $45\nP 2026-11-09 VEQT.TO $45\nP 2026-11-10 VEQT.TO $45\nP 2026-11-11 VEQT.TO $45\n' >prices/VEQT.TO.prices && hledger -f - import --get --dry-run --today 2026-11-12 new.j 2>&1; s=$?; cd /; rm -rf $D; exit $s
no ./data/getdata script, skipping data fetch
no new transactions found in new.j
>=0

# ** 4. A price: tag on a commodity directive overrides: three words,
# SOURCE TICKER QUOTE, name the ticker and the commodity its prices are in,
# used without the checks, and several such tags are several pairs to
# fetch; one word is the commodity's market code, from which tickers are
# inferred as for any other.
<
commodity VEQT ; price: yahoo VEQT.TO $
commodity XIU ; price: XIU.TO
commodity btc ; price: yahoo BTC-USD usd, price: yahoo BTC-CAD $
commodity $ ; price: CAD

2026-10-05 buy
    assets:broker      10 VEQT @ $45
    assets:broker      10 XIU @ $40
    assets:cash      $-850

2026-10-06 buy
    assets:crypto     0.001 btc @ $100000
    assets:cash      $-100

$ D=$(mktemp -d) && cd $D && touch new.j && hledger -f - import --get --dry-run --today 2026-11-12 new.j 2>&1; s=$?; cd /; rm -rf $D; exit $s
no ./data/getdata script, skipping data fetch
would run: yahoo VEQT.TO 2026-09-28..2026-11-11 >./prices/VEQT.prices
would run: yahoo XIU.TO or XIU.TO-CAD 2026-09-28..2026-11-11 >./prices/XIU.prices
would run: yahoo BTC-USD 2026-09-29..2026-11-11 >./prices/btc.prices
would run: yahoo BTC-CAD 2026-09-29..2026-11-11 >./prices/btc.prices
would run: yahoo USDCAD=X or USD or USD-CAD 2026-09-29..2026-11-11 >./prices/usd.prices
no new transactions found in new.j
