# ** 6. A malformed price: tag is an error, before any price is fetched.
<
commodity VEQT.TO ; price: yahoo VEQT.TO

2026-10-05 buy
    assets:broker      10 VEQT.TO @ $45
    assets:cash      $-450

$ D=$(mktemp -d) && cd $D && hledger -f - get --prices --dry-run 2>&1; s=$?; cd /; rm -rf $D; exit $s
hledger: Error: commodity VEQT.TO has a malformed price: tag, "yahoo VEQT.TO": it should be a market code (one word) or SOURCE TICKER QUOTE (three words)
>=1

# ** 7. A price: tag naming the ecb source fetches the euro reference rates
# of the European Central Bank: USD-CAD is the price of 1 USD in CAD. A
# reference rate is final when it is published, so its days are wanted up
# to today, where Yahoo's end yesterday.
<
commodity $ ; price: CAD
commodity usd ; price: ecb USD-CAD $

2026-10-01 buy
    assets:broker      10 XIU.TO @ $50
    assets:cash      $-500

2026-10-02 usd
    assets:usd        100 usd @ $1.40
    assets:cash      $-140

$ D=$(mktemp -d) && cd $D && touch new.j && hledger -f - import --get --dry-run --today 2026-11-12 new.j 2>&1; s=$?; cd /; rm -rf $D; exit $s
no ./data/getdata script, skipping data fetch
would run: yahoo XIU.TO or XIU.TO-CAD 2026-09-24..2026-11-11 >./prices/XIU.TO.prices
would run: ecb USD-CAD 2026-09-25..2026-11-12 >./prices/usd.prices
no new transactions found in new.j
>=0

# ** 8. A price: tag naming the coinbase source fetches the daily candles of
# a Coinbase product, the price of a day being the close of its UTC day:
# BTC-USD's, the price of 1 BTC in USD. Its days are wanted up to yesterday,
# as Yahoo's, and as Coinbase refuses a request spanning more than 300 days,
# a longer run is asked for in pieces of 300 days, each a request of its
# own. usd, the quote, is left to Yahoo.
<
commodity $ ; price: CAD
commodity btc ; price: coinbase BTC-USD usd

2025-06-01 opening
    assets:cash      $5000
    equity:opening  $-5000

2025-06-02 usd
    assets:usd       1000 usd @ $1.40
    assets:cash     $-1400

2025-06-03 btc
    assets:crypto    0.01 btc @ 100000 usd
    assets:usd      -1000 usd

$ D=$(mktemp -d) && cd $D && touch new.j && hledger -f - import --get --dry-run --today 2026-11-12 new.j 2>&1; s=$?; cd /; rm -rf $D; exit $s
no ./data/getdata script, skipping data fetch
would run: coinbase BTC-USD 2025-05-27..2026-03-22 >./prices/btc.prices
would run: coinbase BTC-USD 2026-03-23..2026-11-11 >./prices/btc.prices
would run: yahoo USDCAD=X or USD or USD-CAD 2025-05-26..2026-11-11 >./prices/usd.prices
no new transactions found in new.j
>=0
